<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $24.66 bln on March 14.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $24.66 bln on March 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $24.66 billion on March 14, 1997 from $24.08 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Mar 14	Mar 7	  Mar 15</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     20,680	20,097	 16,802</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,977	 3,977	  4,659</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	     2		9</p>
<p>    Total			     24,659	24,076	 21,470</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
